                        "entry_id": "ed105b49-c97a-37b5-a73f-3dfdc7807d61",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Describes a condition or process involving both fibrous tissue formation and bleeding."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6cfa509c-75f2-486a-9a11-f12fb92ca5f0",
                                "sense_id": "aed91ed8-7689-36d4-9ee7-10e99b1dd61d",
                                "text": "Intraperitoneal injections of a strong solution produce fibrohemorrhagic peritonitis of varying intensity, according to the strength of the solution; while intraperitoneal injections of small quantities of a diluted solution of formalin induce a chronic peritonitis with great connective tissue proliferation, and a striking eosinophilia."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9c89fbbb-d10b-4621-94b0-9a53d1ce9a0a",
                                "sense_id": "aed91ed8-7689-36d4-9ee7-10e99b1dd61d",
                                "text": "If a large fibrohemorrhagic complex had to be removed via a large retinectomy, a silicon oil tamponade is preferable."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d82eac77-ad99-47af-8d70-3e1c59f30085",
                                "sense_id": "aed91ed8-7689-36d4-9ee7-10e99b1dd61d",
                                "text": "A finrinous or fibrohemorrhagic can develop the second or third day following a transmural infarct and usually will resolve."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
